**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** The pure halves of AssignSlot and SwapSlot: which items fit a slot, what a slot becomes when it holds one, how a dial reading is drawn and recorded, and which setup a swap lands on (001 §P `AssignSlot`, `SwapSlot`; 001 §J 'Quick swap: … each dropdown lists compatible items only; choosing one is either a new setup or an existing one'; 001 §I 'Experiments record raw dial readings, and the zero is an ordinary parameter'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.2. (1) The number a parameter holds now, moved where a slot can read it. (a) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs`: `ParameterState` (step 214) gains `member this.currentValue : ParameterValue`, a `KnownParameter`'s value, an `UnknownParameter`'s `start` and a `CalibratedParameter`'s `value`: the rule step 245 wrote into `ParameterValues.ofParameters`, moved, so `ofParameters` (`ItemEvaluation.fs`) maps each parameter through `state.currentValue` and its answers are unchanged. (b) `ParameterValue.angle` (step 246, an extension in `ItemEvaluation.fs`) moves to `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ItemModels.fs` as an intrinsic member of `ParameterValue` (step 207), its body and doc unchanged, deleted from `ItemEvaluation.fs`; its readers there keep calling it. (c) In `Kit.fs`, after `Item` (step 215): `type Item with member this.dialZeroAngle : Angle` is the `currentValue.angle` of the item's `ParameterName.dialZero` parameter (step 244), and `Angle.zero` when it has none (a fixed item). (2) `Setups.fs`, after step 257's members. (a) `type ItemModelChoice with member this.libraryEntryOpt : LibraryEntry option`: `SourcePresetChoice (sourceModel, s)` is `Some (SourceItem s)`, `PolarizerPresetChoice (polarizerModel, p)` `Some (PolarizerItem p)`, `StackSampleChoice (_, s)` `Some (SampleItem s)` and `LibraryModelChoice _` `None`: the library entry a table element is bound to when the item sits on it (`ElementId.fs:LibraryEntry`). `member this.slotKinds : CatalogueKind list` is, for a library entry, its `forKinds` (`ElementId.fs:LibraryEntry`, the rule the table's binding already applies), and for an item model its form's (step 208): `RealPolarizerModel` [`LinearPolarizer`]; `RetarderPlateModel` [`LinearPolarizer`; `CircularPolarizer`; `Sample`]; `BlackBoxMuellerModel` [`Sample`]; `CompoundModel` [`LinearPolarizer`; `CircularPolarizer`], as the compound polarizer presets fit both; `EmptySlotModel` [`LinearPolarizer`; `CircularPolarizer`; `Sample`]; and the three detector models [`Detector`], with no wildcard arm. (b) `type SetupSlot with`: `member this.withItem (item : Item) (model : ItemModelChoice) : Result<SetupSlot, SetupError>` answers `IncompatibleSlotItemErr` naming the item's label and the slot's kind when `model.slotKinds` lacks the slot's `placement.catalogueKind`; otherwise the slot holding `ItemInSlot (item.id, turn)`, `turn` being `DialTurn (sign.readingOf item.dialZeroAngle placement.r1)` for `DialMounted sign` (so the drawn angle is kept) and `PlacementTurn` for `FixedMounting`; when `model.libraryEntryOpt` is `Some entry`, the placement's `valueId` becomes `Some entry.entryId` and its emission `Library.placementEmissionForEntry placement.emission entry` (`ElementId.fs:placementEmissionForEntry`), exactly as the table binds an entry (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:withBoundSampleEmission`), so the drawn element and its item agree; an item model leaves the binding as it is. `member this.withoutItem : SetupSlot` holds `EmptySlotContent` and keeps the placement. `member this.drawnWith (items : Item list) : SetupSlot`: a `DialTurn reading` slot whose item is in `items` with `DialMounted sign` has R1 `sign.physicalAngleOf item.dialZeroAngle reading`; every other slot is unchanged. `member this.recordedWith (items : Item list) : SetupSlot` is its inverse: such a slot's reading becomes `sign.readingOf item.dialZeroAngle placement.r1`. The table turns a slot in physical angles, and the setup records the reading. (c) `SetupSwap` = `SwitchToHeldSetup of Setup` | `CreateSwappedSetup of Setup`. `type Setup with static member swapTarget (slots : SetupSlot list) (held : Setup list) (fresh : SetupName) : SetupSwap` answers `SwitchToHeldSetup` of the first held setup whose current slots hold, slot by slot in order, the same `placement.catalogueKind` and `content` as `slots`, and otherwise `CreateSwappedSetup` of `{ name = fresh; revision = SetupRevision.first; slots = slots; history = [] }`. Nothing writes; the host records (steps 263, 264). No other member is added. Tests, in `SetupTests`: `an item fits the slots its model may fill`: the `slotKinds` and `libraryEntryOpt` of `SourcePresetChoice` of `BuiltinCatalogue.source PresetIds.heNe633`, of the `PresetIds.polarizerLp` polarizer, of `StackSampleChoice` of `SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId` at version 1, and of `LibraryModelChoice` of each of the eight built-in item models (`BuiltinCatalogue.itemModel`, step 210), as listed above. `an item put in a slot binds the slot to its library entry, and a dial-mounted item keeps the drawn angle as its reading`: into a `LinearPolarizer` slot at R1 30°, a `FixedMounting` item of the LP preset gives `ItemInSlot (id, PlacementTurn)` bound to `PresetIds.polarizerLp`; a `DialMounted DialNegative` item of it whose `dialZero` is known at 10° gives `DialTurn (−20°)`, and that slot `drawnWith [ item ]` keeps R1 30°; a glass-plate item into a `Sample` slot binds the sample's entry id and its `supportedEmission`; a real-LP item-model item keeps the slot's `valueId`; a source item into the polarizer slot answers `IncompatibleSlotItemErr` naming its label; and `withoutItem` holds `EmptySlotContent` with the placement unchanged. `a dial reading is drawn through the item's current zero, and the table's angle is recorded back as a reading`: that dial slot drawn after the item's `dialZero` is set to 20° (`withParameterState`, step 234) has R1 −1 · (−20° − 20°) = 40°; the slot turned to R1 50° and `recordedWith [ item ]` holds `DialTurn (−30°)`; a `PlacementTurn` slot is unchanged by both; all within 1e-12. `a swap switches to the held setup holding that content, and otherwise makes a new setup`: over held setups A and B, `swapTarget` of B's slots answers `SwitchToHeldSetup B`; slots no held setup holds answer `CreateSwappedSetup` named `fresh` at revision 1 with no history; and B's slots with one dial reading changed are not matched. In `KitItemTests` (step 213): `a parameter state answers its current number, and an item its dial zero`: `currentValue` of a known 0.1, an unknown starting at 0.5 within [0, 1] and a calibration of 0.25 answer 0.1, 0.5 and 0.25; an item whose `dialZero` is known at π / 18 answers that angle, and a `FixedMounting` item `Angle.zero`. `ItemEvaluationTests`' facts pass unchanged. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved.

**Acceptance.** After the pure slot updates land, `ItemModelChoice.slotKinds` MUST name the slots an item fits, `SetupSlot.withItem` MUST bind the slot to the item's library entry and record a dial-mounted item's reading, `drawnWith` and `recordedWith` MUST map readings through the item's current zero, and `Setup.swapTarget` MUST find the held setup with the swapped content or make a new one; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an item fits the slots its model may fill`, `an item put in a slot binds the slot to its library entry, and a dial-mounted item keeps the drawn angle as its reading`, `a dial reading is drawn through the item's current zero, and the table's angle is recorded back as a reading`, `a swap switches to the held setup holding that content, and otherwise makes a new setup` and `a parameter state answers its current number, and an item its dial zero`, the count rising by 5; and build, elevation and the fifteen s26 invariants MUST pass.
